# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
# How to cite NOQTIS. The version follows project() in CMakeLists.txt.
# No doi yet: Zenodo mints one when the first release is published (its
# metadata comes from .zenodo.json); add it here as `doi:` then.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NOQTIS in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "NOQTIS: Notary Of Quantum-safe Traceable Inputs and Seals"
abstract: >-
  NOQTIS is a C11 library and command-line tool, with no dependencies,
  that seals a folder of files (the exact data, code and outputs behind a
  result) with a post-quantum signature, so that anyone can check later,
  offline, that every file is unchanged, that nothing was added or
  removed, and which key sealed it. It implements ML-DSA (FIPS 204),
  SLH-DSA (FIPS 205), ML-KEM (FIPS 203), HQC, SHA-2 and SHA-3, tested
  against the NIST ACVP and Wycheproof test vectors.
authors:
  - alias: rootcoder007
  - name: "The NOQTIS contributors"
version: 0.1.0
# The licence is Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception (see LICENSE); CFF 1.2.0
# takes a single SPDX licence identifier, not an expression, so the
# exception is carried by license-url.
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: "https://github.com/rootcoder007/noqtis/blob/main/LICENSE"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rootcoder007/noqtis"
url: "https://rootcoder007.github.io/noqtis/"
keywords:
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - digital signatures
  - provenance
  - reproducibility
  - ML-DSA
  - SLH-DSA
  - ML-KEM
  - FIPS 203
  - FIPS 204
  - FIPS 205
